SYN = chi(R_i,R_j:F) - chi(R_i:F) - chi(R_j:F).  chiPAR = chi of the parity record R_iR_j.
MARGIN = chiPAR - max(chi_i, chi_j): positive means the fragment knows the RELATION better
than either record it relates.  #pure = pairs where chi_i,chi_j < 0.01 bit but chiPAR > 0.01,
summed over fragments -- the fragment holds the relation and neither relatum.

